                  "content": "SELECTED: candidate_68\n\nCONFIDENCE: HIGH\n\nEXPLANATION:\nThe fix commit renumbers the switch-case fallthrough chain in KeychainDatabase.onUpgrade(),\nremoving an extraneous \"case 7: // consolidate\" that stood alone (doing nothing) immediately\nbefore \"case 8:\" (which creates the CREATE_API_APPS_ALLOWED_KEYS table), and shifting all\nsubsequent case labels (8->7, 9->8, 10->9, ..., 15->14) down by one to match.\n\nThis exact bug was introduced in candidate_68. That diff bumps DATABASE_VERSION from 7 to 8\nand adds the new migration step for the \"api_allowed_keys\" table, but writes it as:\n\n    case 7:\n        // consolidate\n    case 8:\n        // new table for allowed key ids in API\n        try {\n            db.execSQL(CREATE_API_APPS_ALLOWED_KEYS);\n        } catch (Exception e) {\n            // never mind, the column probably already existed\n        }\n\nHere \"case 7:\" was meant to represent the single migration step for the version bump to 8,\nbut a redundant empty \"case 7: // consolidate\" was inserted before the real logic under\n\"case 8:\", introducing an extra, meaningless case label into the fallthrough chain. Since\nswitch-case in onUpgrade() relies on fall-through (each case number corresponding to the\ntarget DB version an upgrade step brings the schema to), this spurious duplicate case\nnumber desynchronizes the case labels from the actual DATABASE_VERSION values used\nthroughout the rest of the method, \"consolidating\" a version that shouldn't exist as\na distinct step. All later commits that added further migration steps (candidates\n69-87 for case 9 through case 15) inherited and built on top of this off-by-one numbering\nwithout correcting the root issue. The fix commit finally removes the bogus standalone\n\"case 7: // consolidate\" and shifts every subsequent case number down by one, restoring\ncorrect alignment between case labels and intended migration/version semantics\n(\"fix ridiculous database migration bug\").\n\nCandidate_68 is the first commit where this erroneous extra case label pattern appears,\nmaking it the bug-introducing commit.\n"
